    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nLATEST POSTS\nABOUT\nCONTRIBUTORS\nCATEGORIES\nSEARCH WILEY CONNECT\nThe FCC's Expanding Role in National Security\nMay 8, 2026\n\nIn this episode of Wiley Connected, Wiley’s Megan Brown is joined by colleagues Sara Baxenberg and Josh Turner to discuss the Federal Communications Commission’s (FCC) growing role in national security. They explore how recent FCC actions, ranging from supply chain oversight to equipment authorization and enforcement, are reshaping expectations for manufacturers, infrastructure providers, and businesses across industries. The conversation highlights what companies should be watching and why FCC developments now matter far beyond traditional telecom regulation.\n\nThis is the first installment of Signal Shift, a wireless-focused video and podcast series that explores the legal, policy, and market forces reshaping the ecosystem. Through short videos and conversations, Wiley attorneys examine the decisions, technologies, and market trends influencing wireless connectivity, infrastructure, spectrum, and communications policy in the United States and globally.\n\nCategories\nSpectrum Policy\nWiley Connected Podcast\nTags\nEquipment Authorization\nFCC\nInfrastructure\nNational Security\nSpectrum\nWireless\nWireless Networks\nWiley Connect\nSign up for updates\nSubscribe\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nFirm\nCareers\nInclusion and Engagement\nHome\nSite Map\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nCookies Policy & Settings\nCalifornia Privacy Notice\n© 2026 Wiley Rein LLP All Rights Reserved.\nSubscribe\n\nOur Site uses cookies to improve your experience. Cookies may collect your personal information, such as IP address or device identifier, which we may disclose to our analytics partners. You may opt out of the cookies that are not strictly necessary if you wish. By using this site, you agree to our updated Privacy Policy, Terms & Conditions, and Cookies Policy.\n\nCUSTOMIZE COOKIE CHOICES\nREJECT ALL COOKIES\nACCEPT ALL COOKIES"
